      {
        "rank": 7,
        "evidence_text": "\uf0a7 Water-cooled six-cylinder boxer engine\n\n\uf0a7 Max. power: 382 kW (520 hp) at 8,400 rpm; Max. torque: 470 Nm at 6,150 rpm; Max. rpm: 8,750 rpm\n\n\uf0a7 Displacement 3,996 cm \u00b3; stroke 81.5 mm; bore 102 mm\n\n\uf0a7 Camshafts with extended valve opening times\n\n\uf0a7 Intake manifold with two resonance flaps\n\n\uf0a7 Flow optimized single throttle butterfly system\n\n\uf0a7 Dry-sump lubrication with oil-water heat exchanger\n\n\uf0a7 Engine control unit Bosch MS 6.6 with integrated Porsche Motorsport Traction Control (PMTC) and Push-2-Pass functionality\n\n\uf0a7 Race exhaust system with DMSB certified catalytic converter\n\n\uf0a7 Single-mass flywheel\n\n\uf0a7 Fuel quality: Superplus unleaded, to E20 (min. 98 octane); E-Fuels ready (compliant with Article 266 of FIA Appendix J)\n\nOnly engines sealed in accordance with Article 2.11.1 of these regulations are permitted to be used in the Series.Engines can be called in and inspected at any time by the Scrutineers or on the instructions of the Stewards.",
